# Hosts that execute keel's linux/amd64 vector code, one per line.
#
# Copy to .keel-hosts (gitignored) and edit. Requirements per host:
#   - amd64 with AVX2+FMA, and for the AVX-512 backend the F/CD/BW/DQ/VL
#     bundle that archsimd.X86.AVX512() gates on
#   - sshd with key auth from this machine
#   - a Go toolchain and OpenBLAS: the P3 reference is built and run natively on
#     every gate host, so both halves of the ratio come from one invocation on
#     one machine (the ruling on issue #23 retired the separate reference-host
#     list, which is why there is no .keel-openblas-hosts any more)
#   - for P2/P3 benchmark numbers, a clock established stable by whichever
#     instrument the host has: the `performance` governor where `cpufreq` is
#     readable, else BenchmarkPeak sampled head/middle/tail (§5 rule 5 as
#     amended 2026-08-16 — a virtualized guest has no governor to set)
#
# Or set KEEL_REMOTE_HOSTS="host-a host-b", which takes precedence.
# See docs/hosts.md.
#
# One more machine-local list, same format, read by scripts/gate-p3.sh:
#
#   .keel-sentinel  ($KEEL_SENTINEL_HOST) — the host P2's throughput floor is
#     re-checked on, to notice a K-loop that P3 made fatter. Should be the host
#     that classifies issue-bound, since that is where instruction count binds.
#     Empty means every host is a sentinel: missing configuration costs time,
#     never coverage.

# zen4.example.internal
# skylake-x.example.internal
